# Table chrome

Use shared classes from `src/lib/table-styles.ts` (CSS in `globals.css`). Do not invent one-off table frames or header backgrounds.

## Two families

| Family | Classes | When |
|---|---|---|
| **Calendar grids** | `TABLE_SHELL`, `TABLE_FRAME`, `TABLE_HEADER`, `TABLE_HEADER_*`, `TABLE_BODY` | Week plan, Month calendar, Season planner **timeline** |
| **Editorial data tables** | `DATA_TABLE_SHELL`, `DATA_TABLE` (+ `data-density`), `DATA_CELL_*`, `DATA_NUM` | Races, Results, Personal bests, sparse list tables |

## Data table rules

- Continuous surface: white sheet (`#FFFFFF`) on white page — **no** heavy outer box, **no** vertical cell borders; hierarchy from horizontal dividers only
- Header: Manrope 11–12px / 600 / uppercase / `letter-spacing: 0.04em` / secondary gray / **white** bg
- Rows: white; dividers `#E5E7EB`; hover `#FAFAF9`; selected `rgba(244,81,30,.05)` + orange left edge
- Densities: comfortable ~56–64px / compact ~48–52px
- Primary cell text vs secondary hierarchy; numbers use `DATA_NUM` (`tabular-nums` + semibold)
- Status → `StatusPill`; Priority → `PriorityBadge`; Sport → `SportDot` / icon + label (not full-row color)
- Poster typography (`TablePosterHeading`) goes **above** the table, never inside cells

## Calendar grid rules

- Frames are **square** (`rounded-none`)
- Week plan uses `TABLE_FRAME` on `<table>`
- Prefer importing constants over duplicating border strings
- Add new variants only in `globals.css` + `table-styles.ts`
